1. What is Git?

Definition: Git is a Distributed Version Control System (DVCS) used to track changes in files and manage different versions of a project.
Simple Telugu: Git అంటే Project లో జరిగిన Changes ని Track చేసి ప్రతి Version ని Store చేసే Software

2. What is Version Control?

Without Git:Very confusing. 
Project
│
├── final.java
├── final_new.java
├── final_latest.java
├── final_latest2.java

With Git:Git manages every version.
Project
│
├── Commit 1
├── Commit 2
├── Commit 3

3. What is a Repository?

A Repository is a project managed by Git.
When you execute: git init (Git creates a hidden folder:) --> .git (This folder stores all Git information.)

What does git init do? 
It creates a hidden .git directory. Inside .git, Git stores:
Commit History
Branches
Configuration
Logs
Repository Metadata
HEAD

Important: git init does not start tracking files automatically.

How to verify a Git Repository? 
Method 1: git status --> If it shows: On branch master/On branch Main , It is a Git Repository.
Method 2: ls -la If you see .git It is a Git Repository.

4. Working Directory
The Working Directory is where you create or edit files.
The changes are only in your Working Directory,Nothing is saved into Git yet.

5. Staging Area
git add filename --> Move selected changes to the Staging Area.
Think of it as: Ready for Commit.

6. Commit
git commit -m "message" -->  Commit creates a permanent snapshot of your project.
Every commit has:Commit ID
Author
Date
Commit Message

7. Git Workflow
Working Directory
        │
        ▼
git add
        │
        ▼
Staging Area
        │
        ▼
git commit
        │
        ▼
Local Repository

8. git status 
Most frequently used command, Shows:
Current Branch
Untracked Files
Staged Files
Modified Files
Commit Status

9. git init vs git clone
git init : Creates a new empty repository --> creates .git
git clone : Downloads an existing repository (git clone <repository-url>)

Clone automatically:

Downloads project files
Downloads .git
Configures the remote repository (origin)
----------------------------------------->No need to run git init after cloning.
